 عَلَيْكُمْ جُنَاحٌ أَنْ تَبْتَغُوا فَضْلاً مِنْ رَبِّكُمْ‏}‏ فِي مَوَاسِمِ الْحَجِّ‏.‏\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSahih al-Bukhari 1643 - Hajj (Pilgrimage) - كتاب الحج - Sunnah.com - Sayings and Teachings of Prophet Muhammad (صلى الله عليه و سلم) (https://sunnah.com/bukhari%3A1643)\nciteturn27view2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1643\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://sunnah.com/bukhari:1643; Total lines: 85\nL0: Contribute to our mission 【0†Donate Now】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Qur'an†quran.com】 | 【2†Sunnah】 | 【3†Prayer Times†salah.com】 | 【4†Audio†quranicaudio.com】\nL3: \nL4: 【5†Image: toggle Light Thme】 【6†Image: toggle Dark Thme】\nL5: \nL6: [Input: Search …] [Input]\nL7: ## Select Collections\nL8: \nL9: Sahih al-Bukhari\nL10: \nL11: Sahih Muslim\nL12: \nL13: Sunan an-Nasa'i\nL14: \nL15: Sunan Abi Dawud\nL16: \nL17: Jami` at-Tirmidhi\nL18: \nL19: Sunan Ibn Majah\nL20: \nL21: Show More Collections\nL22: \nL23: [Button: Apply]\nL24: \nL25: Quotes e.g. \"pledge allegiance\"\nL26: Searches for the whole phrase instead of individual words\nL27: \nL28: Wildcards e.g. test*\nL29: Matches any set of one or more characters. For example test* would result in test, tester, testers, etc.\nL30: \nL31: Fuzzy Search e.g. swore~\nL32: Finds terms that are similar in spelling. For example swore~ would result in swore, snore, score, etc.\nL33: Term Boosting e.g. pledge^4 hijrah\nL34: Boosts words with higher relevance. Here, the word pledge will have higher weight than hijrah\nL35: \nL36: Boolean Operators e.g. (\"pledge allegiance\" OR \"shelter) AND prayer\nL37: Create complex phrase and word queries by using Boolean logic.\nL38: \nL39: 【7†More ...】\nL40: \nL41: 【2†Home】 » 【8†Sahih al-Bukhari】 » 【9†Hajj (Pilgrimage) - كتاب الحج】 » Hadith 1643\nL42: \nL43: Language:\nL44: \nL45: [Input] English\nL46: \nL47: [Input] Urdu  اردو\nL48: \nL49: [Input] Bangla  বাংলা\nL50: \nL51: كتاب الحج\nL52: \nL53: 25\nL54: \nL55: Hajj (Pilgrimage)\nL56: \nL57: (79)\nL58: Chapter: The Tawaf (Sa'i) between As-Safa and Al-Marwa\nL59: \nL60: (79)\nL61: \nL62: باب وُجُوبِ الصَّفَا وَالْمَرْوَةِ وَجُعِلَ مِنْ شَعَائِرِ اللَّهِ\nL63: \nL64: Sahih al-Bukhari 1643\nL65: \nL66: Narrated `Urwa:\nL67: I asked `Aisha : \"How do you interpret the statement of Allah,. : Verily! (the mountains) As-Safa and Al-Marwa are among the symbols of Allah, and whoever performs the Hajj to the Ka`ba or performs `Umra, it is not harmful for him to perform Tawaf between them (Safa and Marwa.) (2.158). By Allah! (it is evident from this revelation) there is no harm if one does not perform Tawaf between Safa and Marwa.\" `Aisha said, \"O, my nephew! Your interpretation is not true.\nL68: Had this interpretation of yours been correct, the statement of Allah should have been, 'It is not harmful for him if he does not perform Tawaf between them.' But in fact, this divine inspiration was revealed concerning the Ansar who used to assume lhram for worship ping an idol called \"Manat\" which they used to worship at a place called Al-Mushallal before they embraced Islam, and whoever assumed Ihram (for the idol), would consider it not right to perform Tawaf between Safa and Marwa.\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nSahih al-Bukhari 4495 - Prophetic Commentary on the Qur'an (Tafseer of the Prophet (pbuh)) - كتاب التفسير - Sunnah.com - Sayings and Teachings of Prophet Muhammad (صلى الله عليه و سلم) (https://sunnah.com/bukhari%3A4495)\nciteturn27view3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://sunnah.com/bukhari:4495\",\"lineno\":null}); Redirected to URL: https://sunnah.com/bukhari:4495; Total lines: 81\nL0: Contribute to our mission 【0†Donate Now】\nL1: \nL2: 【1†Qur'an†quran.com】 | 【2†Sunnah】 | 【3†Prayer Times†salah.com】 | 【4†Audio†quranicaudio.com】\nL3: \nL4: 【5†Ima